IUnknown}{ to get a pointer to another of the object's interfaces.
\par Because multiple applications can share the same Voice Command site, changing a site attribute affects all applications registered to use the site, not just
 the application making the change. To receive notification of attribute changes, an application must specify the VCMDRF_ALLMESSAGES value when calling the }{\b IVoiceCmd}{::}{\b Register}{
 member function. Note that attribute settings are saved between uses of the site, even if the computer is shut of
\par The application must call the }{\b IVoiceCmd}{::}{\b Register}{ member function before it can call any of the functions in IVCmdAttributes. 
\par A Voice Command application may not need to use IVCmdAttributes functions if a voice-navigation application is installed on the user's computer. The voice-navigation application typically monitors and controls the attributes of a Voice Command site.

