A Voice Dictation object manages the use of dictation by all voice-aware applications on a user's computer. The Voice Dictation object represents a Voice Dictation site, consisting of an audio device and a speech recognition mo
de provided by an engine. Internally, a Voice Dictation site consists of two DirectSpeechRecognition objects: a speech recognition engine object and an audio source. 
\par The Voice Dictation object can use any speech recognition engine that supports dictation or limited-domain grammars.
\par }\pard\plain \s2\li-360\sb120\sa120\sl-440\slmult0\keep\keepn\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\outlinelevel1\adjustright \fs40\kerning28\cgrid {\cf1 Created by}{
\par }\pard\plain \s16\sa120\sl-240\slmult0\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\adjustright \fs20\cgrid {You create a Voice Dictation object by calling the }{\b CoCreateInstance}{
 function with the CLSID_VDct class identifier and the IID_IVoiceDictation interface identifier. }{\b CoCreateInstance}{ returns a pointer to the }{\b IVoiceDictation}{ interface for the Voice Dictation object.
\par }\pard\plain \s2\li-360\sb120\sa120\sl-440\slmult0\keep\keepn\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\outlinelevel1\adjustright \fs40\kerning28\cgrid {\cf1 Interacts with}{
\par }\pard\plain \s16\sa120\sl-240\slmult0\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\adjustright \fs20\cgrid {The Voice Dictation object calls an application's }{\b IVDctNotifySink}{
 interface to notify the application of speech-related events. Therefore, an application must create a COM object that supports the }{\b IVDctNotifySink}{ interface and must pass the address of the interface to the Voice Dictation object when calling the 
}{\b IVoiceDictation}{::Register member function. The application developer determines how the functions in the interface respond to notifications.
\par The Voice Dictation object will try to use }{\b ISRResGraphEx}{ and }{\b ISRResAudioEx}{ to get the alternatives and audio. If this fails, it will try to use }{\b ISRResBasic}{, }{\b ISRResMerge}{, and }{\b ISRResAudio}{
 for the alternatives. Failing this it resorts to just }{\b ISRResBasic}{ and }{\b ISRResAudio}{.
