For a text-to-speech engine, if there's more than one pronunciation, the highest ranked pronunciation becomes the preferred pronunciation. If there's only one pronunciation, this removes the word from
 the exceptions dictionary (if it's there), and reverts to the LTS rules.
\par For a speech recognition engine, }{\b\cf1 Remove}{\cf1  removes a pronunciation from the backup lexicon. If the last pronunciation was removed, then the user-exception dictionary (backup lexicon) en
try is deleted. The engine may still have a letter-to-sound lexicon entry, which it will use if the word appears in a CFG later.
\par For a speech recognition grammar object (dictation or limited-domain only), }{\b\cf1 Remove}{\cf1  removes the pronunciation from the topic's pronunciation database. If the last pronunciation is removed, the word is removed from the topic.
