This pair of rules causes quotes to work. The first string indicates that a word after a quote snuggles up to the quote. The next two lines cause quotes to alternate between a word before the quote
 snuggling or not. Without this rule, the phrase, "he said quote hello quote" becomes "He said " hello"". With it, "He said "hello"".
\par \page }{\cs80\v\cf6 <!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC "-//IETF//DTD HTML//EN">}{\fs28 Voice Dictation API }{
