\par }\pard\plain \s16\sa120\sl-240\slmult0\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\adjustright \fs20\cgrid {To use voice text, you need to create a Voice Text object and register your application with the object. You create a Voice 
Text object by calling the }{\b CoCreateInstance}{ function with the CLSID_VTxt class identifier and the IID_IVoiceText interface identifier. You must create a separate Voice Text object for each site that your application needs to use. 
\par }{\b CoCreateInstance}{ returns a pointer to the }{\b IVoiceText}{ interface for the Voice Text object. Before an application can perform other Voice Text tasks, it must register itself by calling the }{\b IVoiceText}{::}{\b Register}{ member function. }{
\b Register}{ specifies the site that the object uses for audio output, and passes the address of the application's Voice Text notification interface to the Voice Text object. 
\par The following example shows how to create a Voice Text object and register the application with the object.
\par The function initializes OLE, creates a Voice Text object, and registers the application with the object. It returns TRUE if successful or FALSE otherwise. It uses the following global variables:
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\s65 \f3\fs20\cgrid \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}}\pard\plain \s65\fi-300\li300\sa120\sl-240\slmult0\widctlpar\tx300{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls75\pnrnot0\pnf3\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnhang{\pntxtb \'b7}}\ls75\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
{\i gpIVTxt}{ -- address of }{\b IVoiceText}{ interface 
