\par }\pard\plain \s16\sa120\sl-240\slmult0\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\adjustright \fs20\cgrid {The Voice Text object calls an application's }{\b IVTxtNotifySink}{
 interface to inform the application of Voice Text events so that the application can respond to them. To receive notifications, the application must create a COM object that supports }{\b IVTxtNotifySink}{
 and must pass the address of the interface to the Voice Text object when calling the }{\b IVoiceText}{::Register member function. 
\par The }{\b IVTxtNotifySink}{ interface consists of a set of member functions that correspond to Voice Text events
. When an event occurs on the Voice Text site that the application is using, the Voice Text object calls the member function that corresponds to the event. The application developer determines how the member functions process the event notifications.

\par The following example shows how to define an object class that implements the }{\b IVTxtNotifySink}{ interface.
