"InitialBuf" under "[Settings]" -- Number of milliseconds (of memory) originally allocated for storing the digital audio. Applications should allocate enough memory that 80% of the recordings will take less than the allotted time. 
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\s65 \f3\fs20\cgrid \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}}\pard \s65\fi-300\li300\sa120\sl-240\slmult0\widctlpar\tx300{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls75\pnrnot0\pnf3\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnhang{\pntxtb \'b7}}\ls75\adjustright {
"ReallocBuf" under "[Settings]" -- If the audio recording exceeds the amount of memory originally allocated (by the "InitialBuf" settings), then the buffer is expanded by this many milliseconds. 
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\s65 \f3\fs20\cgrid \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}}\pard \s65\fi-300\li300\sa120\sl-240\slmult0\widctlpar\tx300{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls75\pnrnot0\pnf3\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnhang{\pntxtb \'b7}}\ls75\adjustright {
"MaxBuf" under "[Settings]" -- Maximum amount of time that will be recorded. This defaults to 10000. 
