ISRGramCommon}{::Activate member function to activate the newly created grammar. 
\par }\pard\plain \s16\sa120\sl-240\slmult0\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\adjustright \fs20\cgrid {
The function initializes OLE, creates the speech recognition objects, and activates a grammar. It returns TRUE if successful, or FALSE otherwise. The function uses the following global variables:
