\par }\pard\plain \s16\sa120\sl-240\slmult0\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\adjustright \fs20\cgrid {Enumerates the speech recognition modes supported by a particular engine. An app
lication does not interact with the engine enumerator directly; instead, it uses the speech recognition enumerator, which passes function calls to the engine enumerator. The engine enumerator is supplied by the engine vendor. 
\par }\pard\plain \s2\li-360\sb120\sa120\sl-440\slmult0\keep\keepn\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\outlinelevel1\adjustright \fs40\kerning28\cgrid {\cf1 Created by}{
\par }\pard\plain \s16\sa120\sl-240\slmult0\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\adjustright \fs20\cgrid {The engine enumerator is created when the application calls the }{\b ISRFind}{
::Find member function on a speech recognition enumerator. The application passes the address of an }{\b SRMODEINFO}{ structure that indicates the desired characteristics of the mode and the address of an }{\b SRMODEINFORANK}{
 structure that indicates the relative importance of each characteristic. As an alternative, the application can call member functions of the }{\b ISREnum}{ interface to enumerate the modes.
\par The speech recognition enumerator creates an engine enumerator for each engine registered on the system and passes the call to each engine enumerator.
\par }\pard\plain \s2\li-360\sb120\sa120\sl-440\slmult0\keep\keepn\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\outlinelevel1\adjustright \fs40\kerning28\cgrid {\cf1 Interacts with}{
\par }\pard\plain \s16\sa120\sl-240\slmult0\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\adjustright \fs20\cgrid {
When an engine enumerator receives a Find call from the speech recognition enumerator, the engine enumerator searches its list of speech recognition mode
s for the closest match to the characteristics specified with Find. (If the engine enumerator does not support the }{\b ISRFind}{ interface, it uses the }{\b ISREnum}{ interface to scan the list.)
\par If the engine enumerator locates an appropriate speech recognition mode, it returns the address of an }{\b SRMODEINFO}{ structure that contains information about the mode, including its GUID. The application then calls the }{\b ISRFind}{
::Select member function with this GUID to select the mode and create an engine object.
\par Once an engine object exists, the engine enumerator is no longer needed. The engine enumerator is released automatically when the application releases the speech recognition enumerator.
\par }\pard\plain \s2\li-360\sb120\sa120\sl-440\slmult0\keep\keepn\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\outlinelevel1\adjustright \fs40\kerning28\cgrid {\cf1 Interfaces}{
\par }\pard\plain \s16\sa120\sl-240\slmult0\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\adjustright \fs20\cgrid {The engine enumerator should support the }{\b ISREnum}{ interface and may support the }{\b ISRFind}{
 interface. The engine enumerator may support other interfaces defined by the engine vendor to provide additional functionality.
\par }\trowd \trbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw30\brdrcf11 \trbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw30\brdrcf11 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw30\brdrcf11 \clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw15\brdrcf11 \cltxlrtb \cellx919\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw30\brdrcf11 \clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw15\brdrcf11 \cltxlrtb 
