ate a speech recognition enumerator, call CoCreateInstance function with the CLSID_SREnumerator class identifier and the IID_ISRFind or IID_ISREnum interface identifier, depending on the interface desired.
\par CoCreateInstance returns the address of the requested interface on the newly created speech recognition enumerator.
\par }\pard\plain \s2\li-360\sb120\sa120\sl-440\slmult0\keep\keepn\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\outlinelevel1\adjustright \fs40\kerning28\cgrid {\cf1 Interacts with}{
\par }\pard\plain \s16\sa120\sl-240\slmult0\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\adjustright \fs20\cgrid {
When a speech recognition enumerator is created, it loads the registry entries for each engine installed on the system and creates an engine enumerator object to represent each engine. 
\par The application calls the }{\b ISRFind}{::Find member function on the speech recognition enumerator with the address of an }{\b SRMODEINFO}{ structure that indicates the desired characteristics of the mode and the address of an }{\b SRMODEINFORANK}{
 structure that indicates the relative importance of each characteristic. As an alternative, the application can call member functions of the }{\b ISREnum}{ interface to enumerate the modes.
\par The speech recognition enumerator passes these calls to each engine enumerator until one of them returns a mode that fits the requested characteristics.
\par After the application has created an engine object, the speech recognition enumerator is no longer needed and the application can release it.
\par }\pard\plain \s2\li-360\sb120\sa120\sl-440\slmult0\keep\keepn\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\outlinelevel1\adjustright \fs40\kerning28\cgrid {\cf1 Interfaces}{
