To create a speech recognition sharing object, call the CoCreateInstance function with the CLSID_SRShare class identifier and an IID_IEnumSRShare interface identifier. 
\par The CoCreateInstance function returns the address of an }{\b IEnumSRShare}{ interface on the newly created speech recognition sharing object.
\par }\pard\plain \s2\li-360\sb120\sa120\sl-440\slmult0\keep\keepn\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\outlinelevel1\adjustright \fs40\kerning28\cgrid {\cf1 Interacts with}{
\par }\pard\plain \s16\sa120\sl-240\slmult0\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\adjustright \fs20\cgrid {The application enumerates the available engine/audio-source pairs by calling member functions of the }{\b IEnumSRShare}{ interface on the
 speech recognition sharing object. These member functions return addresses of }{\b SRSHARE}{ structures with information about each pair, including its instance identifier.
\par To select an existing pair, the application calls the }{\b IEnumSRShare}{::Share member function with the instance identifier of the desired pair.
\par To create a new pair, the application calls the }{\b IEnumSRShare}{::New member function with the GUID of a speech recognition mode and the device identifier of an audio source that is not currently in use.
\par Both Share and New return addresses of the }{\b ISRCentral}{
 interface on the engine of the pair. After obtaining this interface, the application interacts with the engine as though it had connected directly with it and can release the speech recognition sharing object.
\par When a speech recognition sharing object is used to share an audio source among several engines, the object provides exclusive rights to the source to one engine at a time on a first-come, first-served basis. An engine requests the audio source by calli
ng the }{\b IAudio}{::Start member function. If more than one engine requests the audio source at a time, the first engine to call }{\b IAudio}{::Start is awarded exclusive use of the source until that engine calls }{\b IAudio}{::Stop.
\par }\pard\plain \s2\li-360\sb120\sa120\sl-440\slmult0\keep\keepn\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\outlinelevel1\adjustright \fs40\kerning28\cgrid {\cf1 Interfaces}{
