The value of the noise floor, in negative decibels. For example, a value of 30 indicates an energy floor of -30 dB. The noise floor is the noise value in the signal-to-noise ratio (SNR) for a particular environment. In general, the higher the noise value 
in the ratio, the more sensitive the speech recognition engine is to background noise. For example, a quiet office would have a high SNR (low floor), whereas a noisy factory would have a low SNR (high floor).\cell }\pard\plain 
