\par Because ISRFind selects a spe
ech recognition mode based on the relative importance of various characteristics, it may not always select the optimal mode (just as the Windows font-matching function does not always select the optimal font). ISRFind is best used to select a default spee
ch recognition mode. An application should also allow the user to select a mode, and should store its GUID so that the mode can be retrieved later.
\par The ISRFind interface for the speech recognition enumerator calls ISRFind for all of the registered speech re
cognition engines and then selects the closest result. If an engine does not supply an ISRFind interface, the speech recognition enumerator uses the engine's }{\b ISREnum}{ interface to simulate this functionality.
\par The ISRFind interface is provided by the speech recognition enumerator and engine-enumerator objects and has these member functions:
\par Find 
