The ISRGramNotifySink interface is used by a speech recognition engine to notify an application of recognition-related events. An application specifies the address of this interface when it 
creates the grammar object. A grammar may or may not call the PhraseHypothesis and Training member functions.
\par An engine processes one "phrase" at a time and follows every PhraseStart member function with a PhraseFinish member function before going on to pr
ocess the next phrase. This means that the engine may fall behind in recognitions if several phrases or commands are spoken in quick succession. However, the application need not be concerned about this. If the engine is paused, it does not go on to the n
ext phrase.
\par The ISRGramNotifySink interface must match the }{\b ISRCentral}{ interface from which the GrammarLoad member function is being called -- ISRGramNotifySinkA for ISRCentralA (ANSI) or ISRGramNotifySinkW for ISRCentralW (Unicode).
\par The ISRGramNotifySink interface is supported by an application. It has these member functions:
\par BookMark (some speech engines may not support this function) 
\par Paused 
\par PhraseFinish 
\par PhraseHypothesis (some speech engines may not support this function) 
\par PhraseStart 
\par ReEvaluate (some speech engines may not support this function) 
\par Training (some speech engines may not support this function) 
\par UnArchive (some speech engines may not support this function for context-free or limited domain grammars) 
\par }\pard\plain \s2\li-360\sb120\sa120\sl-440\slmult0\keep\keepn\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\outlinelevel1\adjustright \fs40\kerning28\cgrid {\cf1 BookMark}{
