\par A graph is defined as a set of nodes. Each node has zero or more arcs connecting the node to other nodes. For the ISRResGraphEx interface, each node stores temporal information, such as the time, and each arc stores a \ldblquote word\rdblquote 
 and other information, such as pronunciation. Arcs and n
odes can also store other information. Each arc and node is identified by a unique DWORD. Arcs are divided into two categories: those connecting to nodes to the right of the current node (in the future) and those connecting to nodes to the left (in the pa
st). 
\par A graph can have only one starting node and only one ending node. The starting node has no arcs to the left, while the ending node has no arcs to the right.
\par The ISRResGraphEx interface is supported by the speech recognition results object and has these member functions:
