\par }\pard\plain \s16\sa120\sl-240\slmult0\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\adjustright \fs20\cgrid {
Enumerates the text-to-speech modes supported by a particular engine. An application does not interact with the engine enumerator directly; instead, it uses 
the text-to-speech enumerator, which passes member function calls to the engine enumerator. The engine enumerator is supplied by the engine vendor. 
\par }\pard\plain \s2\li-360\sb120\sa120\sl-440\slmult0\keep\keepn\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\outlinelevel1\adjustright \fs40\kerning28\cgrid {\cf1 Created by}{
\par }\pard\plain \s16\sa120\sl-240\slmult0\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\adjustright \fs20\cgrid {The engine enumerator is created when the application calls the }{\b ITTSFind}{::Find member function o
n a text-to-speech enumerator. The application passes the address of a }{\b TTSMODEINFO}{ structure that indicates the desired characteristics of the mode and the address of a }{\b TTSMODEINFORANK}{
 structure that indicates the relative importance of each characteristic. As an alternative, the application can call }{\b ITTSEnum}{ member functions to enumerate the modes.
\par The text-to-speech enumerator creates an engine enumerator for each engine registered on the system and calls each engine enumerator.
\par }\pard\plain \s2\li-360\sb120\sa120\sl-440\slmult0\keep\keepn\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\outlinelevel1\adjustright \fs40\kerning28\cgrid {\cf1 Interacts with}{
\par }\pard\plain \s16\sa120\sl-240\slmult0\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\adjustright \fs20\cgrid {When an engine enumerator receives a }{\b ITTSFind}{
::Find call from the text-to-speech enumerator, the engine enumerator searches its list of text-to-speech modes for the closest match to the characteristics specified by Find. (If the engine enumerator does not support the }{\b ITTSFind}{
 interface, it uses the }{\b ITTSEnum}{ interface to scan the list.)
\par If the engine enumerator locates an appropriate text-to-speech mode, it returns the address of an }{\b TTSMODEINFO}{ structure that contains information about the mode, including its GUID. The application then calls the }{\b ITTSFind}{
::Select member function with this GUID to select the mode and create an engine object.
\par Once an engine object exists, the engine enumerator is no longer needed. The engine enumerator is released automatically when the application releases the text-to-speech enumerator.
\par }\pard\plain \s2\li-360\sb120\sa120\sl-440\slmult0\keep\keepn\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\outlinelevel1\adjustright \fs40\kerning28\cgrid {\cf1 Interfaces}{
\par }\pard\plain \s16\sa120\sl-240\slmult0\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\adjustright \fs20\cgrid {The engine enumerator should support the }{\b ITTSEnum}{ interface and may support the }{\b ITTSFind}{
 interface. The engine enumerator may support other interfaces defined by the engine vendor to provide additional functionality.
