\par }\pard\plain \s16\sa120\sl-240\slmult0\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\adjustright \fs20\cgrid {
Enumerates the text-to-speech modes provided by all of the engines available to the application. The application uses the text-to-speech enumerator t
o select a text-to-speech mode and create an engine object to represent that mode within the application. The text-to-speech enumerator is supplied by Microsoft.
\par }\pard\plain \s2\li-360\sb120\sa120\sl-440\slmult0\keep\keepn\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\outlinelevel1\adjustright \fs40\kerning28\cgrid {\cf1 Created by}{
\par }\pard\plain \s16\sa120\sl-240\slmult0\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\adjustright \fs20\cgrid {To create a text-to-speech enumerator, call the CoCreateInstance function with the 
CLSID_TTSEnumerator class identifier and the IID_ITTSFind or IID_ITTSEnum interface identifier, depending on the interface desired.
\par CoCreateInstance returns the address of the requested interface on the newly created text-to-speech enumerator.
\par }\pard\plain \s2\li-360\sb120\sa120\sl-440\slmult0\keep\keepn\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\outlinelevel1\adjustright \fs40\kerning28\cgrid {\cf1 Interacts with}{
\par }\pard\plain \s16\sa120\sl-240\slmult0\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\adjustright \fs20\cgrid {
When a text-to-speech enumerator is created, it loads the registry entries for each engine installed on the system and creates an engine enumerator object to represent each engine. 
\par The application calls the }{\b ITTSFind}{::Find member function on the text-to-speech enumerator with the address of a }{\b TTSMODEINFO}{ structure that indicates the desired characteristics of the mode and the address of a }{\b TTSMODEINFORANK}{
 structure that indicates the relative importance of each characteristic. As an alternative, the application can call }{\b ITTSEnum}{ member functions to enumerate the modes.
\par The text-to-speech enumerator passes these calls to each engine enumerator until one of them returns a mode that fits the requested characteristics. 
\par After the application has created an engine object, the text-to-speech enumerator is no longer needed and the application can release it.
\par }\pard\plain \s2\li-360\sb120\sa120\sl-440\slmult0\keep\keepn\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\outlinelevel1\adjustright \fs40\kerning28\cgrid {\cf1 Interfaces}{
