\par }\pard\plain \s16\sa120\sl-240\slmult0\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\adjustright \fs20\cgrid {This section describes, in alphabetical order, the interfaces and functions that support DirectTextToSpeech.
\par In addition to the interfaces described in this section, each object supports }{\b IUnknown}{, which is a common interface supported by all OLE component objects. A speech recognition engine may also support }{\b ILexPronounce}{ or }{\b ILexPronounce2}{
, optional interfaces that allow a user to correct words in the engine's pronunciation lexicon. 
\par DirectTextToSpeech interfaces contain functions that allow an application to implement text-to-speech. There are the following interfaces:
\par }{\b ITTSAttributes}{ 
\par }{\b ITTSBufNotifySink}{ 
\par }{\b ITTSCentral}{ 
\par }{\b ITTSDialogs}{ 
\par }{\b ITTSEnum}{ 
\par }{\b ITTSFind}{ 
