noise value in the ratio, the more sensitive the speech recognition engine is to background noise. For example, a quiet office would have a high SNR (low floor), whereas a noisy factory would have a low SNR (high floor).\cell }\pard\plain 
\widctlpar\intbl{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\adjustright \fs20\cf14\cgrid {\cf0 \row }\pard\plain \s16\sa120\sl-240\slmult0\widctlpar\intbl{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\adjustright \fs20\cgrid {SRATTR_LEVEL (DWORD)\cell 
The record level, with the low word being the left channel, and high word the right channel. Engines will just call down to IAudio::LevelGet or LevelSet. Changing the value through the IAttributes interface allows the engine to expect a level change.
\cell }\pard\plain \widctlpar\intbl{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\adjustright \fs20\cf14\cgrid {\cf0 \row }\pard\plain \s16\sa120\sl-240\slmult0\widctlpar\intbl{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\adjustright \fs20\cgrid {
SRATTR_LISTENINGSTATE (DWORD)\cell Defaults to 0. \line \line 
If non-zero, stops the speech recognition engine from listening to any grammar, although the grammars are not deactivated. This is different than pause, because when the engine is paused, it's still recording. Applications can
 also use a state of non-zero to temporarily free up wave-in device for other purposes. \line \line An application can use this to turn speech recognition on/off quickly without having to activate/deactivate all the grammars. \line \line 
Applications should increment this number to stop the speech recognition from listening. And decrement it, to resume listening. \cell }\pard\plain \widctlpar\intbl{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\adjustright \fs20\cf14\cgrid {\cf0 \row 
}\pard\plain \s16\sa120\sl-240\slmult0\widctlpar\intbl{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\adjustright \fs20\cgrid {SRATTR_MICROPHONE (STRING)\cell The name of the current microphone. \cell }\pard\plain 
\widctlpar\intbl{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\adjustright \fs20\cf14\cgrid {\cf0 \row }\pard\plain \s16\sa120\sl-240\slmult0\widctlpar\intbl{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\adjustright \fs20\cgrid {SRATTR_REALTIME (DWORD)\cell 
The real-time setting for the engine. The real-time setting is the percenta
ge of processor time that the engine expects to use during constant speech. For most engines, the amount of processor time required diminishes markedly during periods of silence. For example, if the real-time setting is 100, the engine takes one full minu
t
e of processor time to process one minute of speech. If the real-time setting is 50, the engine takes 30 seconds of processor time to process the same minute of speech. This value is difficult to compute precisely, so it should be regarded as an estimate.
\cell }\pard\plain \widctlpar\intbl{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\adjustright \fs20\cf14\cgrid {\cf0 \row }\pard\plain \s16\sa120\sl-240\slmult0\widctlpar\intbl{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\adjustright \fs20\cgrid {
SRATTR_RESULTSINFO (DWORD)\cell A listing of which results object information is currently being collected. The following flags are defined: 
\par SRRI_AUDIO - Digital audio is stored. If the SRRI_AUDIO_UNCOMPRESSED bit is not set, then the digital audio may be compressed and of lower fidelity then the audio which the recognizer captured. 
\par SRRI_AUDIO_UNCOMPRESSED - If this flag is set and SRRI_AUDIO is set, then the audio stores in the same fidelity as that which was passed into the recognizer. 
\par SRRI_ALTERNATIVES - Alternative hypothesis are stored. 
\par SRRI_WORDGRAPH - Results graph (of words) is being stored. 
\par SRRI_PHONEMEGRAPH - Phoneme graph is being stored.\cell }\pard\plain \widctlpar\intbl{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\adjustright \fs20\cf14\cgrid {\cf0 \row }\pard\plain \s16\sa120\sl-240\slmult0
\widctlpar\intbl{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\adjustright \fs20\cgrid {SRATTR_RESULTSINFO_POSSIBLE (DWORD)\cell A listing of what results object information can be collected. (Values c
annot be set.) Applications can use this to determine what alternatives are available. It has the same flags as SRATTR_RESULTSINFO.\cell }\pard\plain \widctlpar\intbl{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\adjustright \fs20\cf14\cgrid {\cf0 \row 
