\par }\pard\plain \s16\sa120\sl-240\slmult0\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\adjustright \fs20\cgrid {The ITTSFind interface is supported by the text-to-speech enumerator and the engine enumerator. It has these member functions:
\par Find 
\par Select 
\par The ITTSFind interface allows an application to search through text-to-speech modes to select a mode that most closely matches the desired characteristics and to create an engine object that represents the selected mode. 
\par Because the ITTSFind interface sel
ects a text-to-speech mode based on the relative importance of various characteristics, it may not always select the optimal mode (just as the Windows font-matching function does not always select the optimal font). The ITTSFind interface is best used to 
select a "default" text-to-speech mode. An application should also allow the user to select a mode and should store its GUID so the mode can be retrieved later.
\par The ITTSFind interface for the text-to-speech enumerator uses ITTSFind for all of the registered
 text-to-speech engines and then selects from the closest result. A text-to-speech engine may also supply an ITTSFind interface. However, if it does not, the ITTSFind interface of the text-to-speech enumerator uses the engine's }{\b ITTSEnum}{
 interface to simulate this functionality.
\par }\pard\plain \s2\li-360\sb120\sa120\sl-440\slmult0\keep\keepn\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\outlinelevel1\adjustright \fs40\kerning28\cgrid {\cf1 Find}{
