amp" is actually an index into the number of bytes played/recorded by the audio stream. The time-stamp does not necessarily start at 0. Time stamps only ever increase in value over the life of the audio object, and never decrease in value. Every byte of d
ata that passes through the audio object increases the time stamp. When the audio is UnClaimed the time stamp will not reset to 0. It might increase if the audio object is being time-shared.\cell }\pard\plain 
