lication a baseline from which to calculate when the audio will be played. 
\par For an audio-source object, the value returned by TotalGet includes the total number of bytes recorded from the audio source, but does not include data in the internal buffer of the audio-source object. This gives the application a way of determining at w
hat time an audio recording occurred. 
\par An application should not assume that the value returned by TotalGet changes only with the }{\b\cf1 IAudioDest}{\cf1 ::DataSet or }{\b\cf1 IAudioSource}{\cf1 ::DataGet member function. If the audio device is shared, the value returned by TotalGet inc
