The Speech Tools objects provide common functionality to speed application development. The tools are COM objects that are designed to be used by applications at run-time. This reference describes: simple coding examples, the Speech Tool COM objects, inte
rfaces, data structures, grammar text file format, and log text file format.
\par \page }{\cs80\v\cf6 <!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC "-//IETF//DTD HTML//EN">}{\fs28 Speech Tools API }{
\par }\pard\plain \s1\li-360\sb120\sa120\sl-560\slmult0\keep\keepn\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\outlinelevel0\adjustright \fs52\kerning28\cgrid {\cf1 Introduction To Using The Speech Tools API}{
\par }\pard\plain \s16\sa120\sl-240\slmult0\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\adjustright \fs20\cgrid {This section demonstrates how to use the following Speech Tools:
\par Grammar compiler object 
\par Logging object 
\par Text-to-speech queue object 
\par For more coding examples, see the sample applications provided with the SDK.
\par }\pard\plain \s2\li-360\sb120\sa120\sl-440\slmult0\keep\keepn\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\outlinelevel1\adjustright \fs40\kerning28\cgrid {\cf1 {\*\bkmkstart Grammar}Grammar Compiler Object}{{\*\bkmkend Grammar}
