\par }\pard\plain \s16\sa120\sl-240\slmult0\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\adjustright \fs20\cgrid {(New for SAPI 4.0)
\par An application using the text to speech queue object will create one or mor
e text-to-speech objects that it wishes to use. It then calls CoCreateInstance (..., CLSID_STTTSQueue, ...), and passes reference pointers to the TTS Queue object by calling pISTTTSQueue->TTSAdd(). Each mode is identified by a name. If the application has
 any digital audio recordings it wishes to queue, it calls pISTTTSQueue->WaveAddFromxxx(). The digital audio can be gotten from wave files, memory, resources, or a stream. Each wave is played because each has a "speak" string associated with it.
\par To queue an
d play the audio, the application calls pISTTTSQueue->Speak(), passing in the string to speak and the preferred text-to-speech voice to use. If the speak string matches one of the audio recordings then the audio recording is played instead of the text-to-
speech engine.
\par You can look at the TTSQ.EXE sample application to see the text-to-speech object being used.
\par \page }{\cs80\v\cf6 <!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC "-//IETF//DTD HTML//EN">}{\fs28 Speech Tools API }{
\par }\pard\plain \s1\li-360\sb120\sa120\sl-560\slmult0\keep\keepn\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\outlinelevel0\adjustright \fs52\kerning28\cgrid {\cf1 COM Objects}{
\par }\pard\plain \s16\sa120\sl-240\slmult0\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\adjustright \fs20\cgrid {The tools included with the Speech API are:
\par Grammar Compiler (new for SAPI 4.0) 
\par Logging Object (new for SAPI 4.0) 
\par Microphone Setup Wizard 
\par Phoneme Converter 
\par Text-to-Speech Queue (new for SAPI 4.0) 
\par \page }{\cs80\v\cf6 <!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC "-//IETF//DTD HTML//EN">}{\fs28 Speech Tools API }{
\par }\pard\plain \s1\li-360\sb120\sa120\sl-560\slmult0\keep\keepn\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\outlinelevel0\adjustright \fs52\kerning28\cgrid {\cf1 Grammar Compiler}{
\par }\pard\plain \s16\sa120\sl-240\slmult0\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\adjustright \fs20\cgrid {(New for SAPI 4.0)
\par The grammar compiler objec
t accepts a human-readable text representation of a grammar and compiles it into a format that can be used by speech recognition engines. It also parses a recognition result and returns a command ID or parse string, saving applications the effort of parsi
ng the recognition results themselves.
\par }\pard\plain \s2\li-360\sb120\sa120\sl-440\slmult0\keep\keepn\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\outlinelevel1\adjustright \fs40\kerning28\cgrid {\cf1 Interfaces}{
\par }\pard\plain \s16\sa120\sl-240\slmult0\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\adjustright \fs20\cgrid {
To run the Grammar Compiler Object, the application calls CoCreateInstance on the compiler's object, CLSID_STGramComp, and queries for the }{\b ISTGramComp}{ interface.
\par The Grammar Compiler understands only ISTGramComp.
\par \page }{\cs80\v\cf6 <!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC "-//IETF//DTD HTML//EN">}{\fs28 Speech Tools API }{
\par }\pard\plain \s1\li-360\sb120\sa120\sl-560\slmult0\keep\keepn\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\outlinelevel0\adjustright \fs52\kerning28\cgrid {\cf1 Logging Object}{
\par }\pard\plain \s16\sa120\sl-240\slmult0\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\adjustright \fs20\cgrid {(New for SAPI 4.0)
\par The logging object is generally used by the telephony controls to monitor calls to an IVR system. PC based applications can also use it. The logging object stores a record of the session, including a recording of the digital audio passed into the speech r
ecognizer. (The logging object works in conjunction with telephony controls and the logging audio source.)
\par }\pard\plain \s2\li-360\sb120\sa120\sl-440\slmult0\keep\keepn\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\outlinelevel1\adjustright \fs40\kerning28\cgrid {\cf1 Interfaces}{
\par }\pard\plain \s16\sa120\sl-240\slmult0\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\adjustright \fs20\cgrid {To run the Log Object, the application does a CoCreateInstance on the log's object, CLSID_STLog, and queries for the }{\b ISTLog}{
interface.
\par The logging object understands only ISTLog.
