\par }\pard\plain \s16\sa120\sl-240\slmult0\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\adjustright \fs20\cgrid {
The phoneme converter object converts between an IPA (International Phonetic Alphabet) representation of pronunciation and other (usually more readable) representations
. Phoneme sets are defined by a conversion file. The object provides default phoneme sets for some languages.
\par Applications can use the phoneme converter to display pronunciations to end users.
\par To run the phoneme converter, the application does a CoCreateInstance on the wizard's object, CLSID_STPhoneConv, and queries for the }{\b ISTPhoneConv}{
 interface. It then calls ISTPhoneConv-SetByLang() to specify the character set, and ISTPhoneConv-To/FromIPA() to convert.
\par The Microphone Setup Wizard understands only ISTPhoneConv.
\par \page }{\cs80\v\cf6 <!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC "-//IETF//DTD HTML//EN">}{\fs28 Speech Tools API }{
