\par Edit box with the word, either the contents of pszWord, or blank. As the user types, the radio buttons and next/finish buttons are enabled/disabled. 
\par Group of three radio buttons, "add word," "remove word," and "change pronunciation." The radio buttons will be enabled/disabled depending upon the existence of the word. 
\par "Play" button that has TTS speaking the pronunciation gotten from pUnkLex. If the TTS engine cannot speak the audio then the "play" button is invisible. 
\par Next - Goes onto the next pane in the wizard, for fix pronunciation. This is enabled if add-word or fix-pronunciation are selected. If add-word is selected, then a default pronunciation will be guessed. Next is disabled if "Remove word" is checked. 

\par Finish - Enabled if remove word is enabled. If the user presses this, a message box comes up verifying that the user wants to remove the word. 
\par Cancel - Cancel. 
\par }\pard\plain \s3\sb120\sa120\sl-400\slmult0\keep\keepn\widctlpar{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\outlinelevel2\adjustright \b\f17\fs36\kerning28\cgrid {\cf1 Add word or fix pronunciation}{
