\par Text with the word 
\par Lots of text telling the user what to do. 
\par If there's more than one pronunciation then it contains a drop-down with a list of pronunciations, "Pronunciation 1," "Pronunciation 2", etc. Changing the drop-down changes the sound. Selecting a new pronunciation will cause it to be spoken by TTS. 

\par "Play" button that has TTS speaking the pronunciation gotten from pUnkLex. It plays the currently selected pronunciation. If the TTS engine cannot speak the audio then the "play" button is invisible. 
\par Sounds like edit box & describe how to use - If the user types in text, it guesses the pronunciation. Typing in text will cause TTS to read out the text. Typing in text causes the 
\par Phoneme edit box & description - Shows the phonemes of the pronunciation. If the user types in text, it 1) clears the sounds like box, 2) plays the audio generated by all the phonemes. 
\par Phoneme button - (Next to phoneme edit box) Brings up a small dialog listing the phonemes and allows the user to select one of the phonemes. When selected it plays the phoneme. Has Add and Cancel. 
\par Add pronunciation - Add a pronunciation button. Adds a new pronunciation and changes the drop-down to reflect the new one. The new pronunciation will be a copy of a previous one. 
\par Remove pronunciation - Removes a pronunciation. First asks for verification, and then removes the current pronunciation. This is hidden if there's only one pronunciation. Thus, it's not valid to remove the last pronunciation. 
\par Finish - Saves everything 
\par Cancel - Abort. 
